tle elementor-size-default\">\u2022 Less repairs &amp; Maintenance<\/h2>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-fdc7691 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"fdc7691\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">\u2022 Less taxes, insurance and other annual\/ monthly outgoings related to the asset<\/h2>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-0fbcdb1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"0fbcdb1\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">\u2022 Less depreciation on asset value &amp; write off on furnishing and fixtures<\/h2>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7c8bc88 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"7c8bc88\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">\u2022 The net total of the above divided by the total acquisition cost of the asset (including transfer fees and brokerage charges)<\/h2>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-072dcaa elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"072dcaa\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">\u2022 Is not a single digit yield as RoI too low for real estate with liquidity crunch? How can I get more from a RoI property? The answer is that is capital appreciation<\/h2>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=